{'symbol': 'AMD', 'date': '2020-01-29 20:30:00', 'title': 'AMD Reports Q4 Non-Gaap Earnings Per Share $0.32', 'text': 'AMD REPORTS FOURTH QUARTER AND ANNUAL 2019 FINANCIAL RESULTS.Q4 NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.32.Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.15.Q4 REVENUE $2.13 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $2.11 BILLION.Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $0.31 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.FOR FULL YEAR 2020, AMD EXPECTS REVENUE GROWTH OF APPROXIMATELY 28 TO 30 PERCENT OVER 2019.AMD EXPECTS NON-GAAP GROSS MARGIN TO BE APPROXIMATELY 45 PERCENT FOR 2020.QTRLY COMPUTING AND GRAPHICS SEGMENT REVENUE WAS $1.66 BILLION, UP 69 PERCENT YEAR-OVER-YEAR.ADVANCED MICRO DEVICES- SEES Q1 REVENUE TO BE APPROXIMATELY $1.8 BILLION, PLUS OR MINUS $50 MILLION.EXPECTS NON-GAAP GROSS MARGIN TO BE APPROXIMATELY 46% IN Q1 OF 2020.QTRLY ENTERPRISE, EMBEDDED AND SEMI-CUSTOM SEGMENT REVENUE WAS $465 MILLION, UP 7 PERCENT YEAR-OVER-YEAR.ADVANCED MICRO DEVICES- YEAR-OVER-YEAR INCREASE IN Q1 REVENUE IS EXPECTED TO BE DRIVEN BY STRONG GROWTH OF RYZEN, EPYC AND RADEON PRODUCT SALES.ADVANCED MICRO DEVICES- QTRLY GROSS MARGIN WAS 45 PERCENT COMPARED TO 38 PERCENT A YEAR AGO.Q1 REVENUE VIEW $1.86 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.FY2020 REVENUE VIEW $8.59 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}
