{'symbol': 'AMZN', 'date': '2020-01-29 16:30:00', 'title': 'LVMH says too early to estimate impact of coronavirus', 'text': "LVMH CFO SAYS Q4 REVENUES WERE DOWN AROUND 40 PERCENT IN HONG KONG.LVMH CHAIRMAN SAYS TOO EARLY TO ESTIMATE IMPACT OF CORONAVIRUS.LVMH CHAIRMAN SAYS IF CORONAVIRUS OUTBREAK LASTS A FEW MONTHS THAN IMPACT WON'T BE TOO SIGNIFICANT, IF IT LASTS FOR YEARS THAN IT'S ANOTHER MATTER.LVMH CHAIRMAN SAYS CHINESE GOVERNMENT HAS REACTED IN A VERY MOTIVATED MANNER TO VIRUS OUTBREAK.LVMH CHAIRMAN SAYS NOT INTERESTED IN ANY LUXURY PLATFORM WHICH AMAZON COULD BE READYING.LVMH CHAIRMAN SAYS MONTH OF JANUARY HAS STARTED VERY WELL."}
{'symbol': 'ANTM', 'date': '2020-01-29 09:30:00', 'title': 'Anthem Reports Reports Q4 Earnings Per Share Of $3.62', 'text': 'ANTHEM REPORTS FOURTH QUARTER AND FULL YEAR 2019 RESULTS REFLECTING SOLID PERFORMANCE.Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE $3.62.Q4 REVENUE $27.1 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $27.1 BILLION.Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $3.88 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.Q4 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $3.88.MEDICAL ENROLLMENT TOTALED 41.0 MILLION MEMBERS AT DECEMBER 31, 2019, AN INCREASE OF 1.1 MILLION, OR 2.7 PERCENT, FROM DECEMBER 31, 2018.BENEFIT EXPENSE RATIO WAS 89.0 PERCENT IN Q4 OF 2019, AN INCREASE OF 220 BASIS POINTS FROM 86.8 PERCENT IN PRIOR YEAR QUARTER.FOR FULL YEAR 2019, LOCAL GROUP MEDICAL COST TREND WAS APPROXIMATELY 6.0%.SEES FY 2020 MEDICAL MEMBERSHIP IS EXPECTED TO BE IN RANGE OF 41.9 - 42.3 MILLION.SEES FY 2020 FULLY-INSURED MEMBERSHIP IS EXPECTED TO BE IN RANGE OF 16.0 - 16.3 MILLION.ANTHEM - EXCPECTS LOCAL GROUP MEDICAL COST TREND WILL BE IN RANGE OF 4.0% +/- 50 BASIS POINTS IN 2020, INCLUDING BENEFIT OF IMPROVED PHARMACY COST.SEES FY 2020 BENEFIT EXPENSE RATIO IS EXPECTED TO BE IN RANGE OF 85.8% PLUS OR MINUS 50 BASIS POINTS.SEES FY 2020 OPERATING REVENUE IS EXPECTED TO BE APPROXIMATELY $117 BILLION, INCLUDING PREMIUM REVENUE OF $101 BILLION - $103 BILLION.'}
