{'symbol': 'DOW', 'date': '2020-01-29 09:30:00', 'title': 'Dow Inc Reports Q4 Operating Earnings Of $0.78 Per Share', 'text': 'QUARTERLY GAAP LOSS PER SHARE FROM CONTINUING OPERATIONS $3.14.QUARTERLY OPERATING EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.78.QUARTERLY NET SALES $10.20 BILLION, DOWN 15% VERSUS PRO FORMA RESULTS LAST YEAR.Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $0.74, REVENUE VIEW $10.07 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.QUARTERLY OPERATING EPS EXCLUDES SIGNIFICANT ITEMS OF $3.92/SHARE.SAYS SIGNIFICANT ITEMS RECORDED IN Q4 INCLUDE IMPAIRMENT OF REMAINING COATINGS & PERFORMANCE MONOMERS DEAL-RELATED GOODWILL & CHARGES RELATED TO SADARA.DOW - SIGNIFICANT ITEMS IN Q4 ALSO INCLUDE INTEGRATION AND SEPARATION COSTS, AND TAX GAIN ASSOCIATED WITH SWISS TAX REFORM.QUARTERLY PERFORMANCE MATERIALS & COATINGS NET SALES OF $2.04 BILLION VERSUS $2.27 BILLION.QUARTERLY INDUSTRIAL INTERMEDIATES & INFRASTRUCTURE NET SALES OF $3.25 BILLION VERSUS $3.78 BILLION.QUARTERLY PACKAGING & SPECIALTY PLASTICS NET SALES OF $4.84 BILLION VERSUS $5.90 BILLION.QUARTERLY NET SALES DOWN PRIMARILY DRIVEN BY LOWER LOCAL PRICES IN ALL OPERATING SEGMENTS DUE TO DECLINE IN GLOBAL ENERGY PRICES.QUARTERLY VOLUME DOWN 2% VERSUS PRO FORMA RESULTS LAST YEAR, PRIMARILY DUE TO LOWER HYDROCARBON CO-PRODUCT SALES.QUARTERLY OPERATING EBIT DOWN, REFLECTING MARGIN COMPRESSION IN PACKAGING & SPECIALTY PLASTICS, INDUSTRIAL INTERMEDIATES & INFRASTRUCTURE.SAYS EXPERIENCED SIMILAR ECONOMIC HEADWINDS IN Q4 AS SEEN ALL YEAR, ESPECIALLY IN INDUSTRIAL SECTOR.'}
