{'symbol': 'EBAY', 'date': '2020-01-29 20:30:00', 'title': 'Ebay Inc. Reports Qtrly Non-Gaap EPS Per Diluted Share Of $0.81', 'text': "REPORTS FOURTH QUARTER AND FULL YEAR 2019 RESULTS.Q4 REVENUE $2.8 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $2.81 BILLION.QTRLY GAAP AND NON-GAAP EPS PER DILUTED SHARE OF $0.69 AND $0.81, RESPECTIVELY, ON A CONTINUING OPERATIONS BASIS.DECLARED A QUARTERLY DIVIDEND OF $0.16 PER SHARE, A 14% INCREASE FROM PRIOR QUARTERLY DIVIDEND.EXPANDS SHARE REPURCHASE AUTHORIZATION BY AN ADDITIONAL $5.0 BILLION.EXPECTS  2020 NET REVENUE BETWEEN $10.72 BILLION AND $10.92 BILLION.Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $0.76 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.QTRLY GAAP AND NON-GAAP OPERATING MARGIN OF 21.9% AND 29.3%, RESPECTIVELY.ACTIVE BUYERS GREW BY 2% ACROSS EBAY'S PLATFORMS, FOR A TOTAL OF 183 MILLION GLOBAL ACTIVE BUYERS DURING Q4.SEES 2020 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE FROM CONTINUING OPERATIONS $2.18 - $2.28 AND NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE FROM CONTINUING OPERATIONS $2.95 - $3.05.QTRLY GROSS MERCHANDISE VOLUME WAS $23.3 BILLION, DOWN 5% ON AN AS-REPORTED BASIS AND DOWN 4% ON A FX-NEUTRAL BASIS.MARKETPLACE PLATFORMS DELIVERED $2.2 BILLION OF REVENUE, DOWN 3% ON AN AS-REPORTED BASIS AND DOWN 1% ON A FX-NEUTRAL BASIS DURING Q4.FOR Q1 2020, CO EXPECTS NET REVENUE BETWEEN $2.55 BILLION AND $2.60 BILLION.STUBHUB PLATFORMS DROVE REVENUE OF $321 MILLION, UP 2% ON BOTH AN AS-REPORTED AND A FX-NEUTRAL BASIS DURING Q4.FOR Q1 2020, CO EXPECTS GAAP EARNINGS PER DILUTED SHARE FROM CONTINUING OPERATIONS IN RANGE OF $0.50 - $0.53."}
