{'symbol': 'MCD', 'date': '2020-01-29 15:30:00', 'title': 'McDonald\'s CEO On Coronavirus Says "Its Actual Impact On Our Business Is Going To Be Fairly Small"', 'text': 'MCDONALD\'S - U.S. HAS 70% OF RESTAURANTS THAT HAVE CONVERTED TO EOTF -CONF CALL.MCDONALD\'S CFO - "RETURNING TO GUEST COUNT GROWTH IN THE U.S. REMAINS OUR TOP PRIORITY".MCDONALD\'S CFO - "SLUGGISH INDUSTRY TRAFFIC GROWTH AND UNIT EXPANSION CONTINUE TO FUEL AN AGGRESSIVE BATTLE FOR MARKET SHARE.".MCDONALD\'S - FRANCHISE MARGIN PERCENT DOWN 60 BASIS PTS AS FRANCHISE REVENUE GROWTH WAS OFFSET BY HIGHER DEPRECIATION RELATED TO EOTF IN U.S..MCDONALD\'S - EXPECTS TO SPEND ABOUT $800 MILLION OF CAPITAL TO OPEN ABOUT 400 RESTAURANTS IN CO\'S WHOLLY OWNED MARKETS.MCDONALD\'S CEO- "BREAKFAST IS THE ONLY DAYPART IN THE INDUSTRY THAT\'S SEEING TRAFFIC GROWTH. WE HAVE TO WIN AT BREAKFAST".MCDONALD\'S CEO ON CORONAVIRUS- CO HAS BEEN WORKING WITH LOCAL AUTHORITIES, PARTICULARLY IN HUBEI PROVINCE; CO HAS CLOSED ALL RESTAURANTS IN HUBEI.MCDONALD\'S CEO ON CORONAVIRUS- STILL HAS ABOUT 3,000 OPEN RESTAURANTS IN CHINA; CO HAS PUT IN PLACE EPIDEMIC PREVENTION AND CONTROL TASK FORCE.MCDONALD\'S CEO ON CORONAVIRUS-  CHINA REPRESENTS ABOUT 9% OF GLOBAL RESTAURANT COUNT, ABOUT 4% TO 5% OF SYSTEM-WIDE SALES AND ABOUT 3% OF OP INCOME.MCDONALD\'S CEO ON CORONAVIRUS-  "CHINA IS A CRITICAL MARKET FOR US, AND WE\'RE VERY CONCERNED ABOUT THE SITUATION OVER THERE".MCDONALD\'S CEO ON CORONAVIRUS-  "ITS ACTUAL IMPACT ON OUR BUSINESS IS GOING TO BE FAIRLY SMALL, ASSUMING AGAIN THAT IT STAYS CONTAINED TO CHINA".'}
