{'symbol': 'RCL', 'date': '2020-01-29 12:30:00', 'title': 'Royal Caribbean Estimates Additional 10 Cent/Shr Impact If China Travel Restrictions Continue', 'text': "ROYAL CARIBBEAN COMMENTS ON CORONAVIRUS AND ANNOUNCES DATE OF 4TH QUARTER EARNINGS CALL.ROYAL CARIBBEAN CRUISES - CANCELLED THREE SAILINGS THROUGH FEB 8(TH), ON HIGH YIELDING SPECTRUM OF SEAS, CURRENTLY ITS ONLY SHIP HOMEPORTED IN CHINA.ROYAL CARIBBEAN - IF TRAVEL RESTRICTIONS IN CHINA CONTINUE UNTIL END OF FEB, ESTIMATES THIS WOULD FURTHER IMPACT RESULTS BY ADDITIONAL $0.10/SHARE.ROYAL CARIBBEAN CRUISES LTD - ESTIMATES THAT THIS CANCELLATION WILL IMPACT 2020 FINANCIAL RESULTS BY ABOUT $0.10 PER SHARE.ROYAL CARIBBEAN CRUISES LTD - FOR WINTER SAILING SEASON, CO ONLY HAS ONE SHIP BASED IN CHINA.ROYAL CARIBBEAN - EXPECT EROSION OF CONSUMER CONFIDENCE IN CHINA COULD HAVE ADDITIONAL IMPACT ON LOAD FACTOR, RATE IN REGION UNTIL MARKET NORMALIZES.ROYAL CARIBBEAN CRUISES LTD - FOR ALL OF 2020, CHINA REPRESENTS ABOUT 6% OF COMPANY'S CAPACITY..ROYAL CARIBBEAN - IF CHINA TRAVEL RESTRICTIONS CONTINUE FOR EXTENDED PERIOD OF TIME, THEY COULD HAVE MATERIAL IMPACT ON OVERALL FINANCIAL PERFORMANCE.ROYAL CARIBBEAN CRUISES LTD - FOR WINTER SAILING SEASON IN CHINA, TWO ADDITIONAL SHIPS ARE SCHEDULED TO JOIN  IN MAY AND JULY 2020, RESPECTIVELY."}
