{'symbol': 'SWK', 'date': '2020-01-29 09:30:00', 'title': 'Stanley Black & Decker Reports Full Year And 4Q 2019 Results', 'text': "STANLEY BLACK & DECKER REPORTS FULL YEAR AND 4Q 2019 RESULTS.Q4 REVENUE $3.7 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $3.78 BILLION.SEES FY 2020 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $8.05 TO $8.35.Q4 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.32.Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $2.18 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.EXPECT 2020 ADJUSTED EPS OF $8.80 - $9.00.LOOKING TO 2020 AND BEYOND, WE REMAIN WELL-POSITIONED TO DELIVER SHARE GAINS.REACHES AGREEMENT TO ACQUIRE CONSOLIDATED AEROSPACE MANUFACTURING, LLC (CAM) FOR UP TO $1.5 BILLION.STANLEY BLACK & DECKER - WHEN ADJUSTED FOR ABOUT $185 MILLION OF EXPECTED CASH TAX BENEFITS, NET DEAL VALUE IS APPROXIMATELY $1.1 - $1.3 BILLION.ACQUISITION IS EXPECTED TO BE ACCRETIVE TO EPS BY APPROXIMATELY $0.30 - $0.40 BY YEAR THREE.IN 2020, WE EXPECT TO GENERATE ABOVE-MARKET ORGANIC GROWTH OF APPROXIMATELY 3%.IN 2020, WE EXPECT TO GENERATE ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE EXPANSION OF 5% - 7% VERSUS PRIOR YEAR.2020 FREE CASH FLOW CONVERSION IS EXPECTED TO APPROXIMATE 90%-100% OF GAAP NET INCOME.IN 2020, WE EXPECT TO GENERATE ABOVE-MARKET ORGANIC GROWTH OF APPROXIMATELY 3%.STANLEY BLACK & DECKER-$200 MILLION OF PURCHASE PRICE HELD BACK, CONTINGENT ON BOEING 737 MAX'S FAA AUTHORIZATION, BOEING ACHIEVING SOME PRODUCTION LEVELS.FY2020 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $9.00 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA."}
{'symbol': 'SBUX', 'date': '2020-01-29 22:30:00', 'title': 'Starbucks Says Would Have Raised FY Guidance, If Not For Uncertainty Of Coronavirus Situation', 'text': 'STARBUCKS CORP CEO - GIVEN STRENGTH OF Q1 RESULTS, WE HAD INTENDED TO RAISE CERTAIN ASPECTS OF OUR FISCAL YEAR FINANCIAL OUTLOOK FOR FISCAL 2020.STARBUCKS CORP CEO - HOWEVER, DUE TO DYNAMIC SITUATION UNFOLDING WITH THE CORONAVIRUS, WE ARE NOT REVISING GUIDANCE AT THIS TIME.STARBUCKS CORP CFO - WE SAW TRANSACTION GROWTH IN BOTH THE MORNING AND AFTERNOON DAYPARTS FOR A THIRD CONSECUTIVE QUARTER.STARBUCKS CORP CFO - CHINA BUSINESS REPRESENTED 10% OF GLOBAL REVENUE IN Q1- CONF CALL.STARBUCKS CORP EXEC - WE HAVE DELIVERY AVAILABLE TO CUSTOMERS FROM STORES REMAINING OPEN IN CHINA. BUT THIS IS SOMETHING WE CONTINUE TO ASSESS.STARBUCKS CORP EXEC - WE WOULD HAVE RAISED FY GUIDANCE ON OPERATING MARGIN AND EPS, IF NOT FOR UNCERTAINTY OF CORONAVIRUS SITUATION.STARBUCKS CORP EXEC - WE WILL BE INTRODUCING A BREAKFAST SANDWICH THIS YEAR WITH A PLANT-BASED PATTY, BOTH IN U.S. AND CANADA.'}
{'symbol': 'SBUX', 'date': '2020-01-29 20:30:00', 'title': 'Starbucks Reports Q1 Non-Gaap Earnings Per Share $0.79', 'text': 'STARBUCKS REPORTS Q1 FISCAL 2020 RESULTS.Q1 NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.79.Q1 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.74.Q1 REVENUE $7.1 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $7.11 BILLION.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $0.76 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.Q1 COMPARABLE STORE SALES UP 5% GLOBALLY, LED BY 6% COMP GROWTH IN U.S. AND 3% COMP GROWTH IN CHINA.FISCAL YEAR 2020 GUIDANCE IS UNCHANGED FROM WHAT WAS PROVIDED IN CONJUNCTION WITH ITS Q4 FISCAL 2019 EARNINGS REPORT.IN QUARTER, ACTIVE STARBUCKS REWARDS MEMBERSHIP IN U.S. UP 16% YEAR-OVER-YEAR TO 18.9 MILLION.STARBUCKS - AS WE BEGIN Q2, WANT TO ACKNOWLEDGE DYNAMIC SITUATION OUR PARTNERS IN CHINA ARE NAVIGATING AS HEALTH OFFICIALS RESPOND TO CORONAVIRUS.REMAIN OPTIMISTIC AND COMMITTED TO LONG-TERM OPPORTUNITY IN CHINA.CURRENTLY, WE HAVE CLOSED MORE THAN HALF OF OUR STORES IN CHINA.CONTINUE TO MONITOR AND MODIFY OPERATING HOURS OF ALL OF OUR STORES IN CHINA MARKET IN RESPONSE TO OUTBREAK OF CORONAVIRUS.STARBUCKS - WILL UPDATE ITS GUIDANCE FOR FISCAL 2020 WHEN WE CAN REASONABLY ESTIMATE IMPACT OF CORONAVIRUS.STARBUCKS - CORONAVIRUS DISRUPTION EXPECTED TO MATERIALLY AFFECT OUR INTERNATIONAL SEGMENT AND CONSOLIDATED RESULTS FOR Q2 AND FY OF FISCAL 2020.STARBUCKS REWARDS LOYALTY PROGRAM GREW TO 18.9 MILLION ACTIVE MEMBERS IN U.S., UP 16% YEAR-OVER-YEAR IN QUARTER.'}
